# Force-text source extensions so git's auto-detect heuristic (which
# trips on any embedded \x00 byte) doesn't silently switch to binary
# mode. Real-world example that motivated this file: editor-literal-
# types.js once had a raw NUL inside a cache-key string literal —
# git treated the whole file as binary, `grep` without `-a` skipped
# it, and three downstream popovers looked dead from the outside
# even though they worked at runtime. The file was un-binary'd in
# a follow-up commit (escape sequence instead of raw byte), but
# this attributes file keeps the failure from recurring silently.

*.clj   text diff
*.cljc  text diff
*.cljs  text diff
*.edn   text diff
*.js    text diff
*.mjs   text diff
*.cjs   text diff
*.css   text diff
*.html  text diff
*.svg   text diff
*.md    text diff
*.sql   text diff
*.sh    text diff
*.bb    text diff
